{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"money: cent rounding for ledgers.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef round_cents(amount):\n    \"\"\"Round a decimal amount to cents, halves away from zero.\"\"\"\n    # Multiply by 100 to shift cents to integer\n    shifted = amount * 100\n    # Determine sign\n    sign = 1 if shifted >= 0 else -1\n    abs_shifted = abs(shifted)\n    # Extract integer and fractional parts\n    integer_part = int(abs_shifted)\n    fractional_part = abs_shifted - integer_part\n    # If fractional part is exactly 0.5, round away from zero\n    if abs(fractional_part - 0.5) < 1e-12:\n        rounded = integer_part + 1\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, use normal round\n        rounded = round(abs_shifted)\n    # Restore sign and scale back\n    return sign * rounded / 100\n","expected_sha256":"fa816984cb1f791630c850f452d214933dceee46a979c2276da8800a2c0570db","kind":"modify","path":"src/money.py"}],"rationale":"Replaced the built-in round with custom logic to round halves away from zero as required, preserving the public API and ensuring ledger.total uses this function unchanged."}